        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dorothy Parker, Maxine Kumin, Barbara Swan, Anne Sexton, John Latouche, Lillian Hellman, Stephen Sondheim, John Mauceri, John Wells, Leonard Bernstein\n- Roles: poets, authors, critics, satirists, contributors, collaborators\n- Works: Candide (operetta)\n\nFacts:\n- Dorothy Parker was born on August 22, 1893, and died on June 7, 1967.\n- Dorothy Parker was an American poet, short story writer, critic, and satirist known for her wit, wisecracks, and observations of 20th-century urban foibles.\n- Maxine Kumin was born on June 6, 1925, and died on February 6, 2014.\n- Maxine Kumin was an American poet and author.\n- Dorothy Parker was one of the contributors to the text of Candide, along with John Latouche, Lillian Hellman, Stephen Sondheim, John Mauceri, John Wells, and Leonard Bernstein.\n- Barbara Swan was known for collaborating with the poets Anne Sexton and Maxine Kumin.\n- Barbara Swan was also known for her archived correspondence with various artists and writers.",
